## Cancellation with the archimedean defect

From the archimedean rank-one theorem,

[
\boxed{
H_d^A=R_d^A-2u_du_d^{\mathsf T},
\qquad
R_d^A\succeq0.
}
]

From the prime split above,

[
\boxed{
H_d^P=2u_du_d^{\mathsf T}+R_d^P,
}
]

where (R_d^P) is the contribution of the regular prime part

[
P_{\mathrm{reg}}(s)
===================

# \frac{\eta'}{\eta}(s)

\frac{\zeta'}{\zeta}(s)+\frac1{s-1}.
]

Therefore the completed form is

[
H_d^0
=====

# H_d^A+H_d^P

\left(R_d^A-2u_du_d^{\mathsf T}\right)
+
\left(2u_du_d^{\mathsf T}+R_d^P\right),
]

so

[
\boxed{
H_d^0=R_d^A+R_d^P.
}
]

The pole rank-one terms cancel exactly.

